        "body": "\n\n## Description\n\nAs noticed in https://github.com/jupyterlite/jupyterlite/pull/1822\n\n## Reproduce\n\n- Double click on a CSV file\n- See the following error in the dev tools:\n\n```\nUncaught (in promise) TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'node')\n    at new ea (jlab_core.814c63be63853ada.js?v=814c63be63853ada:22:27835)\n    at new x (jlab_core.814c63be63853ada.js?v=814c63be63853ada:136:6901)\n    at new f (jlab_core.814c63be63853ada.js?v=814c63be63853ada:45:33794)\n    at _.createNewWidget (jlab_core.814c63be63853ada.js?v=814c63be63853ada:45:34135)\n    at _.createNew (jlab_core.814c63be63853ada.js?v=814c63be63853ada:136:6321)\n    at k.createWidget (jlab_core.814c63be63853ada.js?v=814c63be63853ada:131:11407)\n    at T._createOrOpenDocument (jlab_core.814c63be63853ada.js?v=814c63be63853ada:131:22420)\n    at T.open (jlab_core.814c63be63853ada.js?v=814c63be63853ada:131:20367)\n    at T.openOrReveal (jlab_core.814c63be63853ada.js?v=814c63be63853ada:131:20527)\n    at jlab_core.814c63be63853ada.js?v=814c63be63853ada:130:5418\n```\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0573fe0b-2917-4dde-9b1e-930e15f37f83\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nIt should be possible to open CSV with the CSV viewer.\n\n## Context\n\n\n\n- Operating System and version: All\n- Browser and version: Any\n- JupyterLab version: 4.6.0a0\n\n<!--The more content you provide, the more we can help!-->\n\n<details><summary>Troubleshoot Output</summary>\n<pre>\nPaste the output from running `jupyter troubleshoot` from the command line here.\nYou may want to sanitize the paths in the output.\n</pre>\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Command Line Output</summary>\n<pre>\nPaste the output from your command line running `jupyter lab` here, use `--debug` if possible.\n</pre>\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Browser Output</summary>\n<!--See https://webmasters.stackexchange.com/a/77337 for how to access the JavaScript console-->\n<pre>\nPaste the output from your bro